{"action": "shared_understanding_confirmed", "at": "2026-08-28T21:41:28+00:00", "data": {"summary": "The managed-SKU registration slice keeps unmanaged products entirely in Commerce. After Manage Stock is enabled and pool setup is explicitly confirmed, Commerce registers the canonical SKU once at pool scope with logical stock zero and no location balance. Inventory returns a permanent opaque SKU identity while the visible SKU remains the unique pool lookup key. A newly registered Inventory item initializes its display name from the current Commerce Product Title, falling back to the SKU when no title exists; later Inventory and Commerce title changes remain independent. Existing pooled SKUs are never overwritten and continue through the already-locked human review and revalidation path. Set Initial Stock remains a separate location-scoped quantity action. The implementation is limited to the provider-neutral Commerce registration contract, pure state transitions, tests, documentation, and proof; it adds no admin UI, OAuth/discovery, live Inventory transport, stock mutation, checkout, deployment, or production change."}, "event_id": "246bb1e4-b7c7-4993-b4b4-dca4b48ae0d9"}
